scenario offline
expect Terminal sessions
clean
shot welcome
tap-id preview
expect Preview
expect Nothing is running on your computer
clean
expect-state /activity#/effects/fetch 0
expect-state /activity#/effects/post 0
shot preview
tap-id welcome
tap-id setup
expect Pair once
clean
shot setup
expect-missing kobo trust set
tap-id trust
expect Reopen Cobalt once
clean
shot trust
tap-id start
expect Share a terminal
expect kobo stream terminal
expect-missing --interactive
clean
shot start
tap-id enter-address
expect Pair with your computer
clean
shot pairing
type bad address
tap-id kb.enter
expect Use a name or IP address
clean
shot address-error
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
type laptop
tap-id kb.enter
expect Now the pairing code
clean
shot code
type xyz
tap-id kb.enter
expect Enter the six letters and numbers
clean
shot code-error
expect-state /activity#/effects/fetch 0
expect-state /activity#/effects/post 0
tap-id edit-address
expect laptop:9332
tap-id kb.enter
expect xyz
clean
shot code-preserved

# A pairing that has never connected says so, rather than that a connection
# was lost, and names the cause.
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
type abc234
tap-id kb.enter
wait-for This Kobo is not on Wi-Fi.
expect Not connected
expect-missing Connection lost
clean
shot not-connected-yet

# The Pairing menu names the computer and says nothing was saved yet, since
# a pairing is kept only once the computer confirms it.
tap Pairing
wait-for Computer connection
expect laptop:9332
expect Waiting for this computer to confirm pairing.
expect-missing Pairing is saved for next time.
expect-missing Your saved connection
clean
shot pairing-menu
tap Return to terminal
wait-for Not connected
# A computer that does not answer is told apart from a reader off Wi-Fi.
scenario host-down
wait-for Not connected yet. On your computer, run kobo stream terminal.
expect-missing This Kobo is not on Wi-Fi.
clean
shot host-not-answering
# Change computer goes back to the address with the last one in it, and
# the code with the last code.
tap Pairing
wait-for Computer connection
tap Change computer
wait-for Pair with your computer
expect laptop:9332
tap-id kb.enter
wait-for Now the pairing code
expect abc234
# Help on the entry screen opens the steps; the Back buttons under each
# step walk them in order. The top bar's back arrow is also called Back, so
# the buttons are tapped by what they do.
tap Help
wait-for Pair once
tap Next
wait-for Reopen Cobalt once
tap Next
wait-for Share a terminal
# The top bar's back arrow steps back through them as well.
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Reopen Cobalt once
tap Next
wait-for Share a terminal
tap-id trust
wait-for Reopen Cobalt once
tap-id setup
wait-for Pair once
tap-id welcome
wait-for Terminal sessions
# The preview closes back to the first screen, and offers setup too.
tap-id preview
wait-for Preview
tap Connect a computer
wait-for Pair once
tap-id welcome
wait-for Terminal sessions
tap-id preview
wait-for Preview
tap Close preview
wait-for Terminal sessions
# Nothing was confirmed, so a restart opens on the first screen again.
restart
wait-for Terminal sessions
expect-missing Not connected
